msgid "Embed the graph in the text"
msgstr ""

msgid "*Insert embeds that stay live references to the graph.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An embed is a block of the story that shows a part of the graph: a "
"document, a 3D scene, the Matrix of an epoch, a table of units, the "
"epochs on a time axis, the position of the site, the chain of a value. It"
" keeps a reference to a node, never a copy: it is computed from the graph"
" every time the page is drawn, so a unit renamed or moved to another "
"epoch changes in the story as well. What you choose in the block is only "
"how it is shown and its caption."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the story in the Narrative workspace, in **Write** (see :doc:`write-"
"the-narrative`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Insert a block"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Move the pointer between two blocks of a chapter and press the **+** "
"(**Insert a block here**). In an empty paragraph you can also type "
":kbd:`/`: the same menu opens, and the block takes the place of the empty"
" paragraph."
msgstr ""

msgid "The menu **Insert** lists, from the top:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Blocks**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Document** (it shows the thing: photo, PDF, plan, model), **3D scene** "
"(a container, a document with models, an epoch) and **Text**."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Views of the graph**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Matrix** (an epoch's sequence), **Table** (a query on the graph), "
"**Timeline** (the epochs over the years), **Map** (the site's position) "
"and **Paradata** (how a value is reached)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Standard blocks**"
msgstr "**בלוקים סטנדרטיים**"

msgid ""
"**History of research**, **Heritage involved (HDT-O)** and "
"**Bibliography**, which ask the whole file and are recomputed at every "
"opening."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then the gestures **Mention a node**, **AI-assisted draft** and **New "
"chapter here**, and last **Or cite a node**: the nodes of the graph by "
"kind, each shown in the way that suits it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose a kind of block. A second menu, **what it shows**, lists what that"
" block can show. For a **3D scene** it groups **The graph**, the "
"**Epochs**, the **Containers** and the **Documents that publish models**;"
" a single model is found by typing its name. For a **Matrix** choose an "
"epoch, for example *II A.D.*. The **Map** goes straight to the graph's "
"position."
msgstr ""

msgid "Type in the field at the top to search any of these lists."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The block appears where you pressed the **+**, selected, and its "
"**Inspector** opens. ``Edit ▸ Undo`` takes it back."
msgstr ""

msgid "Other ways in"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*From the graph.* Select a node in the Matrix or in the **Outliner** "
"while the story is open: its **Inspector** has a section **In the "
"story**, with **Cite in «chapter»** and the way it will be shown. The "
"block goes at the end of the current chapter. The section also says where"
" the node is already cited."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*A file from the disk.* Drop a file onto a chapter. The form **New "
"document** asks its **ID (e.g. D.1)**, **Description** and **File**; "
"**Create the document** makes the document and shows it in the chapter, "
"as a **3D scene** if the file is a model. The message reminds you to "
"stamp the file in Archive (see :doc:`/how-to/sources/declare-"
"provenance`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*A mention in the text.* Type :kbd:`[[` in a paragraph, or choose "
"**Mention a node**, and pick a node: its name enters the sentence as a "
"mention, which follows the node when it is renamed and counts as a "
"citation in the coverage of the **Index**."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adjust a block in the Inspector"
msgstr ""

msgid "Click a block to select it. Its **Inspector** shows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Shown as**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ways this node can be shown, each with a line that says what changes."
" A document can be shown as **Document** (the image, the PDF page, the "
"text or the models, with its citation) or as **Source** (how this graph "
"uses it: the extractors that read it, what they yield, the criticism of "
"the source)."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Caption**"
msgstr ""

msgid "The text under the block."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Outside EMStudio**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"How the block will come out in the live reader, in Word and LaTeX, and in"
" Jupyter: a figure, a citation with its entry in the bibliography, a link"
" or a query cell."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"▲ and ▼ move the block, and **Delete** removes it. The node itself stays "
"in the graph: what the block says is changed in the node."
msgstr ""

msgid "Some kinds of block have their own controls:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Table**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**The table's question** sets the **Scope** (what the block points at, "
"the units cited in the chapter, the units cited in the text above, or an "
"epoch or an activity), the **Types**, the **Certainty**, the **First "
"epoch**, the **Columns**, the **Order** and the **Direction**. The title "
"and the caption of the table say the scope and the filters."
msgstr ""

msgid "**3D scene**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The scene is loaded only when you ask: the button **▶ Load the scene** "
"says how many objects it holds. A story with many scenes stays light. "
"Turn the view, then press **Save this framing**: the camera and a picture"
" of it are kept in the block, and the picture becomes the figure in Word "
"and LaTeX. **Frame** returns to the saved framing, and **Open in the "
"Space** opens the Space on the scene's epoch with the same camera."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Document**"
msgstr "**מסמך**"

msgid "For a PDF, **Page** chooses the page that the block shows."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Map**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the site has no position yet, the block says **site not positioned**"
" and offers **Set the site position…** (see :doc:`/how-"
"to/space/georeference-a-study`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Scope**, **Include** and **Order** choose which graphs, documents and "
"heritage entities the block lists."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Blocks that stay true to the graph. A Matrix of *II A.D.* shows the units"
" that the epoch's lane holds, with the units whose first epoch is another"
" one marked ↺; a reference whose node has been removed says **unresolved "
"reference** instead of showing something stale. In **Read** a click on a "
"block goes to its node; in **Print** you see the figures and citations "
"the files will carry."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A study from an earlier version may hold blocks that show one model or "
"one unit; they still open, and their **Shown as** keeps those ways."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

